# Urban Table — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is the
# documented list of what exists, and must never contain a real secret.

# ─── Database (REQUIRED) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# PostgreSQL. Everything the restaurant runs on lives here: orders, staff
# accounts, roles, the menu. Without it the application cannot start a request.
#
# The password in this string is a credential. Never rename this variable to
# anything beginning NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that prefix ships the value to every
# visitor's browser. Nothing under src/lib/db may be imported by a client
# component; the browser reaches data through route handlers.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://urbantable:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/urban_table

# TLS. Unset means "verify, unless the host is localhost". Managed providers
# usually need nothing; one whose certificate chain the container lacks needs
# "no-verify" — encrypted but unauthenticated, so it is a deliberate opt-in.
#   require | no-verify | disable
# DATABASE_SSL=

# Connection pool size per process. Behind a serverless platform, where each
# invocation is its own process, set this to 1 and put a pooler (PgBouncer,
# Neon, Supabase) in front. Default 10.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10
# DATABASE_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# Guard on `db:reset`, which truncates every table. Refused in production
# unless this says yes.
# ALLOW_DB_RESET=no

# ─── Address lookup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Postal code → street and city on the checkout address form.
#
# The provider is PDOK Locatieserver, the Dutch Kadaster's own geocoding
# service over the BAG address register. It needs NO API KEY and no account,
# which is why none appears here. It is on by default; every value below is
# optional.

# Which provider to use. "pdok" (default) or "none" to switch lookup off
# entirely — with it off the browser never calls the endpoint at all and every
# address field is typed by hand, exactly as before this existed.
# ADDRESS_LOOKUP_PROVIDER=pdok

# Sent as the User-Agent so the Kadaster can see who is calling and reach you if
# it misbehaves. Their fair-use policy asks for it. Set this before any real
# traffic — an address, not a person: an ops mailbox or the site URL.
# ADDRESS_LOOKUP_CONTACT="Urban Table (ops@example.com)"

# How long to wait before giving up and letting the customer type. Default 3500.
# ADDRESS_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_MS=3500

# Override the service URL — for a mock in tests, or a self-hosted Locatieserver.
# ADDRESS_LOOKUP_URL=https://api.pdok.nl/bzk/locatieserver/search/v3_1/free

# If you ever swap in a keyed commercial provider (Postcode.nl, Loqate, PostNL),
# its key goes here, server-side, and is read only in
# src/lib/fulfillment/address-lookup.ts. Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ —
# that ships it to every visitor.
# ADDRESS_LOOKUP_KEY=

# ─── Staff access ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Seeds the FIRST manager account, once, on a fresh database. It is hashed on
# the way in and never stored as given. After that first seed this variable does
# nothing — the password lives in the database and is changed through the staff
# screens, so removing it from the environment later does not lock anyone out.
#
# Set it before the first `db:seed` on any deployment you care about: the
# fallback is the published default "urbantable".
# ADMIN_PASSCODE=
# SEED_MANAGER_USERNAME=manager

# ─── Development ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Extra hosts allowed to load dev-server internals — a tunnel or staging name.
# Private network addresses already work without this. Development only.
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS="urban-table.ngrok-free.app,*.trycloudflare.com"

# ─── Security headers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HSTS is sent outside development. Set at BUILD time to suppress it, for a
# production build meant to be served over plain HTTP on a LAN.
# HSTS=off
